id: pm-rl-rayz
title: "A promoted generation could store a padded or blank approval identity, consuming none of the budget it was promoted under"
description: "The approved promotion budget is counted by comparing each promoted generation's stored approval to the approval item id with strict equality. The parse boundary trimmed parent but not approval, and accepted an empty approval because it is non-null and so satisfies the promotion-evidence invariant. A generation body carrying an approval of two spaces, or of the approval id with surrounding whitespace, was therefore promoted while matching no approval id and consuming none of that approval's budget."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: budget,identity,refusal
created_at: "2026-08-11T14:44:11.221Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-11T14:46:16.929Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-11T14:46:16.913Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-11T14:46:16.913Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
resolution: "approval is trimmed where parent is trimmed, a blank approval is refused as empty_approval, and the promote command trims its --approval flag so the looked-up id and the stored identity are one string."
expected_result: "A promoted generation whose stored approval is padded consumes the budget of the approval it names, and a blank approval cannot be stored at all."
actual_result: "The padded record is counted (promotion refused with 1 promotion(s) consumed), the blank record makes the budget undecidable and stops the promotion, and all three assertions fail against the reverted implementation."
dependencies[3]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-rl-cnc0,related,"2026-08-11T14:44:20.283Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
  pm-rl-qix7,related,"2026-08-11T14:44:20.283Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
  pm-rl-yi7j,related,"2026-08-11T14:44:20.283Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T14:45:11.132Z","harness:claude-code","Reported by CodeRabbit on unbraind/pm-rl#12 as a Major data-integrity finding, and reproduced before it was applied: parseGenerationSpec trimmed parent at the parse boundary but stored approval verbatim, while countPromotedUnderApproval compares the stored approval to the approval id by strict equality. A hand-authored Generation body is all that is needed; the promote command never has to be called with a padded flag."
  "2026-08-11T14:45:11.702Z","harness:claude-code","Fixed at the parse boundary rather than at the comparison, and a blank approval is refused as empty_approval rather than normalized to null. Normalizing a blank to null would silently downgrade a promoted record to one missing its evidence, so the promotion-evidence invariant would then report a different defect than the one present. The promote command also trims its approval flag so the id it looks up and the identity it stores are the same string."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T14:46:10.489Z","harness:claude-code","An identity that is compared by strict equality must be normalized where it is parsed, not where it is compared, and every such field must be normalized together. This defect existed only because a previous round trimmed parent and stopped there: the same file, the same parse function, the same failure mode, one field later. When a normalization bug is fixed, enumerate every stored identity in the record and fix the class."
  "2026-08-11T14:46:10.865Z","harness:claude-code","A blank value that is non-null passes any invariant written as a null check. The promotion-evidence invariant asks whether approval is non-null, so an empty string satisfied it while matching no approval id - the record was simultaneously promoted-with-evidence and promoted-under-nothing. Presence checks on identity fields must test for a usable identity, not for the absence of null."
files[4]{path,scope,note}:
  index.ts,project,"Approval identity normalized at the parse boundary, the promote flag trimmed to match, and the three assertions that fail against the reverted code."
  lineage.ts,project,"Approval identity normalized at the parse boundary, the promote flag trimmed to match, and the three assertions that fail against the reverted code."
  README.md,project,"Approval identity normalized at the parse boundary, the promote flag trimmed to match, and the three assertions that fail against the reverted code."
  test/lineage.test.ts,project,"Approval identity normalized at the parse boundary, the promote flag trimmed to match, and the three assertions that fail against the reverted code."
tests[2]:
  - command: npm run coverage
    path: test/lineage.test.ts
    scope: project
    note: Parse boundary normalization holds at the 100/100/100 coverage gate
  - command: npm test
    path: test/lineage.test.ts
    scope: project
    assert_stdout_contains[1]: a promoted generation whose stored approval is padded still consumes that approval's budget
    note: Padded approval still consumes its budget
close_reason: "approval is trimmed where parent is trimmed, a blank approval is refused as empty_approval, and the promote command trims its --approval flag so the looked-up id and the stored identity are one string."
